{
 "schema_version": 1,
 "generated": "2026-09-23",
 "policy": "An FAA certificated model (its registry manufacturer spellings, which follow the TC holder history, are listed together) is mapped to an ICAO Doc 8643 designator here only when an FAA document (the model's TCDS or FSB report, or FAA Order JO 7360.1K) ties the FAA model designation, or a marketing name the TCDS or FSB report gives it, to a Doc 8643 record, and every Doc 8643 record so named carries the same designator. A marketing variant inside a named model is accepted (G650ER, Global XRS; the M2 Gen2, which has no serial group of its own); a distinct TC model designation, or a separately approved serial group, whose name Doc 8643 does not carry is not (208B, FALCON 2000EX, FALCON 900EX, DA 50 C: no row, so the lower-authority sources still decide them; the Cessna 525 CJ1+ group and the B300C: unresolved). One model spanning several designators is split by serial number where FAA documents print the split (serial_pattern's group 1 is the number), else recorded as unresolved. Rows here override the name matcher and the OpenSky registration crosswalk, and an unresolved row or an uncovered serial may not be filled by them. Evidence report: docs/aircraft_identity/2026-09-23_faa_model_crosswalk_evidence.md",
